> - Use GitHub ```suggestion blocks when the fix is a concrete replacement of added lines (RIGHT side only — suggestions cannot attach to deleted lines). Where the repo's CI checks formatting, code you suggest, in a suggestion block or a fix's code block, is what its formatter makes of the change in a worktree at the PR head (openmrs-core: `mvn -pl <module> spotless:apply`), not hand-typed: an author commits a suggestion in one click, so a line one column over the limit turns the build red, and a runtime test of the fix misses that when its build skips the formatter. A fix you post is a change you propose: before posting, list for yourself each input and exception type it newly accepts or catches, and read earlier threads on the same lines; where a refutation pass runs, give it the code, not only the claim.
